EU roads are the safest in the world  Parliament voted to improve road safety  even further by making 30 life-saving  technologies mandatory in all new models  from May 20-22  the EU losses up to nine point six  million euros in public procurement each  year due to a lack of whistleblower  protection members voted to ensure  whistleblowers have safe channels to  report wrongdoing consumers should have  the same rights whether buying a product  online or offline including remedies if  a product is defective under new rules  that the trader is liable if a product  becomes faulty within two years of  purchase there are three million EU  workers in gig economy type employment  parliament agreed measures ensuring  better working conditions including  preventing employers from stopping  workers taking other jobs and access to  free training members voted to launch a  nine point two billion euro programme to  shape Europe's future digital  transformation it will help fund  supercomputing AI technology cyber  security and digital skills for citizens
 

